# RETIRED (2026-11-06): the backend's watcher owns keep-alive now; this unit is disabled on the app server and the status
# page no longer checks it. Kept for a manual backstop (docs/testnet-run.md, "Keeping the light clients alive").
# The keep-alive as a cron job, for a machine without the systemd timer (zk-bridge-keepalive.timer is preferred on the
# app server). Install in the crontab of the user that reads backend.json (zkb_backend): crontab -u zkb_backend -e
#
# flock -n skips a run while the last one still waits for a proof (that run exits 1 and is reported like a failure).
# Every line goes to syslog (tag zk-bridge-keepalive). The job prints only when the march exits non-zero, so cron mails
# only then. Exit codes: 12 stranded,
# 3 a read failed, 13 a proof failed, was refused near the deadline, or did not land. Lines that start with
# "ALERT light-client" say which light client and why.
SHELL=/bin/bash
MAILTO=ops@example.invalid
20 */3 * * * cd /opt/zk-bridge/current/explorer/backend && out=$(flock -n /tmp/zk-bridge-keepalive.lock /usr/bin/node bin/zk-bridge-keepalive.mjs march --execute --backend-config /etc/zk-bridge/backend/backend.json --backend-url https://prove.zkb.fi --max-proofs 2 --job-timeout-minutes 90 --head-timeout-minutes 60 2>&1); code=$?; logger -t zk-bridge-keepalive <<<"$out"; [ "$code" -eq 0 ] || { echo "zk-bridge-keepalive: march exit code $code"; grep -E 'ALERT|verdict' <<<"$out"; }
